se.co%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Ftirtha-images%2Fimg_13144.jpeg&amp;w=384&amp;q=75 384w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fiiudzezqkqtqcxbkssdq.supabase.co%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Ftirtha-images%2Fimg_13144.jpeg&amp;w=640&amp;q=75 640w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fiiudzezqkqtqcxbkssdq.supabase.co%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Ftirtha-images%2Fimg_13144.jpeg&amp;w=750&amp;q=75 750w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fiiudzezqkqtqcxbkssdq.supabase.co%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Ftirtha-images%2Fimg_13144.jpeg&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 828w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fiiudzezqkqtqcxbkssdq.supabase.co%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Ftirtha-images%2Fimg_13144.jpeg&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fiiudzezqkqtqcxbkssdq.supabase.co%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Ftirtha-images%2Fimg_13144.jpeg&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fiiudzezqkqtqcxbkssdq.supabase.co%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Ftirtha-images%2Fimg_13144.jpeg&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fiiudzezqkqtqcxbkssdq.supabase.co%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Ftirtha-images%2Fimg_13144.jpeg&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75 2048w, /_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fiiudzezqkqtqcxbkssdq.supabase.co%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Ftirtha-images%2Fimg_13144.jpeg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75 3840w\" src=\"/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fiiudzezqkqtqcxbkssdq.supabase.co%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Ftirtha-images%2Fimg_13144.jpeg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75\"/></div></div><article class=\"prose-none space-y-4 font-body text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.85] text-ink\"><p>Kachholi, Tehsil: Pindwara, Sirohi (Rajasthan)</p><p>Main Deity: The image of Lord Shri Kachchhulika Parshwanath is of white stone, seated in the lotus (padmasana) posture, 29 inches high and 23 inches wide, with a canopy of 7 serpent hoods above its head.</p><p>Location: This temple stands in the center of the village of Kachholi.</p><p>History: In ancient times, Kachholi was a great historic city with prosperous and wealthy merchants. It was founded by the Rao of Kutch, who named it Kachchhulika. An inscription from the year 1343 of the Vikram era attests to the antiquity of this place, so this pilgrimage site is believed to be even older than that. This place is the point of origin of the Kachholiwal gachchha (monastic order). The Parshwanath here is named Shri Kachchhulika Parshwanath after the village of Kachholi, and is also known as Chintamani Parshwanath. This image is ancient and miraculous. Thousands of shravaks (Jain lay followers) lived here in ancient times. Shri Manikyaprabhasuri and Shri Udaysinhsuri of the Kachchhulika gachchha were both conferred the title of Acharya at this very temple. Every year on the 10th day of the bright half of Margashirsha, the temple flag is changed. This temple was renovated in the year 2016 of the Vikram era.</p><p>Other Temples: There is no other temple here.</p><p>Art and Sculpture: The image of the Lord, with its magnificently carved parikar (surrounding frame), is very beautiful and splendid. Beholding this serene and beautiful image, devotees are overcome with emotion and experience great joy.</p><p>Directions: The nearest railway station is Swaroopganj, 5 kilometers away. Bus service and private vehicles are available from here. Vehicles are also available from Mahavir Bhavan in Swaroopganj. Dharmashala and bhojanshala facilities are available here, though it is better to stay in Swaroopganj.</p><p>Scripture References: This temple is mentioned in the &quot;Kachholi Ras,&quot; the &quot;Mangal Kalash Chaupai,&quot; the &quot;Shri Parshwanath Nammala,&quot; the &quot;135 Shri Parshwanath Stavan,&quot; and others.</p><p>Praise (Stuti): Where the Rao of Kutch established the settlement of Kachholi, there the Lord Parshwa was enshrined, taking the name Kachholi; O Kachholi Parshwa, sever the bonds of karma from this worldly existence. &quot;With devotion I bow to Shri Kachchhulika Parshwa.&quot;</p><p>Chanting Mantra: &quot;Om Hrim Arham Shri Kachchhulika Parshwanathaya Namah.&quot;</p><p>Trust: Shri Kachholi Jain Sangh, Post: Kachholi-307023, Station: Swaroopganj, Tehsil: Pindwara, District: Sirohi, State: Rajasthan, India. Phone: 02971-292512, Mobile: 09587225883.</p></article><nav class=\"mt-14 flex items-center justify-between border-t border-sandstone-deep/60 pt-6\"><a class=\"group flex items-center gap-1.5 font-ui text-sm text-ink-soft hover:text-maroon transition-colors\" href=\"/en/tirtha/tirtha-094\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-left h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m15 18-6-6 6-6\"></path></svg><span class=\"max-w-[10rem] truncate sm:max-w-xs\">Shri Posli (Posaliya) Parshwanath</span></a><a class=\"group flex items-center gap-1.5 text-right font-ui text-sm text-ink-soft hover:text-maroon transition-colors\" href=\"/en/tirtha/tirtha-096\"><span class=\"max-w-[10rem] truncate sm:max-w-xs\">Shri Dada Parshwanath</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-right h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"></path></svg></a></nav></div></main><footer class=\"mt-auto border-t border-sandstone-deep/60 py-8\"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 font-ui text-xs text-ink-soft flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-2 sm:items-center sm:justify-between\"><p>१०८ पार्श्वनाथ तीर्थ दर्शन — श्री पार्श्वनाथ भगवान के तीर्थों का डिजिटल संकलन</p><p>Original source: Rajendra Kumar Jain, Parshv Sadan, Parshv Nagar, Dungarpur</p></div></footer><!--$--><!--/$--><script src=\"/_next/static/chunks/40e0f9pufs6g4.js\" id=\"_R_\" async=\"\"></script><script>(self.__next_f=self.__next_f