e is named Shri Kachchhulika Parshwanath after the village of Kachholi, and is also known as Chintamani Parshwanath. This image is ancient and miraculous. Thousands of shravaks (Jain lay followers) lived here in ancient times. Shri Manikyaprabhasuri and Shri Udaysinhsuri of the Kachchhulika gachchha were both conferred the title of Acharya at this very temple. Every year on the 10th day of the bright half of Margashirsha, the temple flag is changed. This temple was renovated in the year 2016 of the Vikram era.. Other Temples: There is no other temple here.. Art and Sculpture: The image of the Lord, with its magnificently carved parikar (surrounding frame), is very beautiful and splendid. Beholding this serene and beautiful image, devotees are overcome with emotion and experience great joy.. Directions: The nearest railway station is Swaroopganj, 5 kilometers away. Bus service and private vehicles are available from here. Vehicles are also available from Mahavir Bhavan in Swaroopganj. Dharmashala and bhojanshala facilities are available here, though it is better to stay in Swaroopganj.. Scripture References: This temple is mentioned in the \\\"Kachholi Ras,\\\" the \\\"Mangal Kalash Chaupai,\\\" the \\\"Shri Parshwanath Nammala,\\\" the \\\"135 Shri Parshwanath Stavan,\\\" and others.. Praise (Stuti): Where the Rao of Kutch established the settlement of Kachholi, there the Lord Parshwa was enshrined, taking the name Kachholi; O Kachholi Parshwa, sever the bonds of karma from this worldly existence. \\\"With devotion I bow to Shri Kachchhulika Parshwa.\\\". Chanting Mantra: \\\"Om Hrim Arham Shri Kachchhulika Parshwanathaya Namah.\\\". Trust: Shri Kachholi Jain Sangh, Post: Kachholi-307023, Station: Swaroopganj, Tehsil: Pindwara, District: Sirohi, State: Rajasthan, India. Phone: 02971-292512, Mobile: 09587225883.\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"1b:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mb-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3\\\",\\\"children\\\"